I actually didn't polypile anything, but zapped a wand of polymorph on
a troll corpse to prevent it from coming back to life. I never
engraved Elbereth either.

I genocided a and S because I wanted to be able to move freely in the
astral plane. The priests are nasty when they call forth uncountable
masses of these beasts, and I like to be able to move around when
dodging Famine and Pestilence who were both looking for me.

Here is the story, as much as I remember it:
Moi was lucky enough to find an altar (Mitra's) in the first level,
and the gnomish mines entry on level 2. Although his pet didn't
survive the falling rock trap in the altar room on the first level...
Moi had a tough time in the mines and early levels of the dungeons
because he couldn't get any decent equipment. A co-aligned altar in
MineTown helped a lot, though, since he could happily zap wands of
create monster and sacrifice with little risks. Still, his +1 dwarvish
mithril coat lasted a long time. Later, he was lucky enough to get
gauntlets of power, and found his bag of holding in Sokoban.
However, Moi reached the quest and Medusa without reflection or magic
resistance, nor a wand of death to get rid of Thoth Amon... A bit of
the quest, and then back to the main dungeons, sacrificing, praying,
and, bad luck, he was crowned early on. A lucky gray dragon gave him a
nice scaly armor. The quest was done, then Moi got rid of Medusa's
titan and Medusa herself. On the way, Moi managed to die once, sunk by
an eel, but his amulet of life saving did the job. He killed Medusa,
went to the castle, went around, blessed-genocided liches and, since
he was at it, mind flayers. In the castle, Moi found the wand of
wishing and rejoiced. So he got scrolls of charging and genocide, used
over the game 3 wishes for blessed figurines of an archon (one at a
time), speed boots, magical hawaiian shirt, blessed magic marker, and
I can't remember what. Later on, Moi would find 3 other wands of
wishing... used 9 wishes in all, but had 3 left, could recharge 2
wands and 2 lamps... He just couldn't think of anything useful.
Moi managed to get a silver shield on the corpse of an angel, and went
into hell after dancing with two nurses in the dungeons of Doom. He
met Yeenoghu, got swallowed by Juiblex, but didn't kill Orcus because
this was a bones file: Orcus had been turned to stone by a previous
Moi who had succumbed to shades that this Moi's silver saber
dispatched. On this corpse did Moi find a lit magic lamp and another
one in the corpse's BoH. The lamp provided light for all my adventure.
At this point, Moi decided he needed a better ascencion kit. He had
lost all his divine protection after an unfortunate prayer, and so
needed it back. His archon pet helped a lot, killing all merchants he
could see (Moi had to lock Istchak in to spare the poor man). The
archon dispatched the priests after they got the money, and Moi
carried thousands and thousands of zorkmids to the 3 priests of the
dungeon (Minetown, one low in the main dungeon and the friendly Moloch
priest below the castle) and got his protection back. He enchanted his
armor as he could, and went down. Dug the vibrating square level
totally before he managed to find out where the square was. Grrr...
Then he went up with his first and most brave archon, genocided the
krakens, and dispatched the Wizard of Yendor with a rubber chicken
that lied nearby handy (had to kill it first of course). The archon
didn't survive the encounter, however, stupidly swallowed by a
trapper. Downward Moi went, opening the passage to the lowest level.
There, a new archon pet helped him dispatch hordes of undeads and
priests, and he genocided serpents and ants. Moi picked up the amulet
of Yendor, and immediately wrote 'THE AMULET OF YENDOR' on it. Up he
went, and Rodney made a guest appearance on this level.
The mysterious force was not that painful this time. Got back 2 levels
twice, to the same level six or seven times, maybe eight at most.
Killed Rodney a few times, including on the first level of the
dungeon, all the times with a wand of death (no use taking risks).
Then Moi entered the plane of earth, killed Rodney with the Vorpal
Sword for a change. Potions of gold detection and scrolls of confusion
(uh, the opposite) were then used. The minotaur's wand of digging got
me to the plane of air in no time. There, I got swallowed by all kinds
of nasty things, resting in the less nasty ones and flying as fast as
possible towards the way out, killing Rodney once more in the process.
The level of fire was full of elementals and other nasties which
decided me to use the ring of conflict. The portal was far away, and 2
archons of Mitra decided that I was unworthy. They summoned tons of
monsters, but I managed to tame a few of these, teleport away others,
and generally escape the lot of monsters to reach the plane of water.
I hate archons when they attack me. Ring of conflict, wands of death
and teleportation, scrolls of taming, and even a potion of full
healing were needed to help my ring of levitation lift me over the
lava up to the plane of water. There, my last scroll showed me the
portal, and I put a ring of free action instead of conflict, and a
ring of protection back instead of levitation. I fought many water
elementals, but managed to get between some of them and reach the
astral plane.
On the Astral plane, I picked the middle door, that of Famine, because
it opened itself alone. I killed a samurai who wielded a +8 Fire
Brand. I tried to get past the various priests and warriors, but they
wer tough, and Pestilence decided to come from the left. I used my
mighty wand  of teleportation and got them out of my way, and dashed
towards the altar. I got blinded somehow, but recognized the altar of
Crom! I sacrificed the Amulet, and the rest, as they say, is history.

